  // Typechecks the TEST TREE, which the root tsconfig.json excludes wholesale.
  //
  // WHY THIS EXISTS. `npm run typecheck`, the `tsc --noEmit` inside predeploy
  // and the lint-staged hook all use the root config, which excludes
  // `tests/**/*`, and vitest does not enable its `typecheck` option. So a
  // TypeScript error under `tests/` was reported by no gate at all. AWTD-908
  // found that the hard way: a compile-time `satisfies` pin in
  // tests/api/v1-contract.test.ts had silently drifted in both directions
  // because nothing was compiling the assertion.
  //
  // A RATCHET, NOT A CLEAN SWEEP (AWTD-916). Turning the whole tree on reports
  // 1318 errors across 193 files. That is a cleanup pass, not a gate anyone
  // can land in one go — so this config covers the tree by DEFAULT and names
  // the files that still fail. 485 of 678 test files are gated today, and
  // every NEW test file is gated automatically, because it is the exclusions
  // that are enumerated rather than the inclusions.
  //
  // TO MAKE PROGRESS: fix a file's type errors, delete its line below, and
  // this gate keeps it fixed. The list only ever shrinks. Do not add to it.
  //
  // THE TWO COMPILER OPTIONS ARE LOAD-BEARING, and between them they account
  // for 155 of the original 1473 errors — i.e. the difference between "1474
  // things are wrong" and the real backlog of 1318:
  //
  //   target: ES2022        47x TS1378, top-level await in test setup. The
  //                         root target is ES6; this is a test-tree concern
  //                         only and does not change what ships.
  //   types: vitest/globals 97x TS2304/TS2593 for `expect`, `it`, `describe`,
  //                         `vi`. Not a fiction: vitest.shared.ts sets
  //                         `globals: true`, so these really are in scope.
  //
  // `types/**/*.d.ts` is not optional — the module augmentation in
  // types/next-auth.d.ts is what gives Session.user its `id`, and without it
  // this config reports phantom errors in lib/ rather than real ones in tests.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "types": ["vitest/globals", "node"]
  },
  "include": ["types/**/*.d.ts", "tests/**/*.ts", "tests/**/*.tsx"],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",

